p right into that way back in the  summer of last year shrimp apple pro  showed us this exclusive iphone 14 pro  display panel from one of apple's  suppliers and as you can see it looks  crazy because you have a pill-shaped  cutout right here and another bigger  cutout right next to it and i think  because of that a lot of people just  wrote it off and completely ignored it  but way back then he said that it was  meant for the iphone 14 with a punch  hole and he said there's a 70 to 80  percent chance that apple would use this  design and then later on in september he  gave us another update saying that the  2022 iphone would likely have this  design mentioning that the camera is on  the right so you can see that little  cutout right there that's for the selfie  camera and then the face id system would  be on the left so that bigger cutout  would house some of the face id sensors  along with some sensors going under here  as well and i do want to remind you guys  that the only reason this is possible is  because with the iphone 13 apple took  the speaker cutout with the built-in  microphone and everything and they put  it up to the top of the frame so it's  essentially going to sit above the  display panel right there and that is  the reason why apple is able to  basically free up this portion this gap  in between the camera and the sensors  and the top of the iphone and now going  back to shrimp apple pros leak he says  that apple is doing it for both the 6.1  inch iphone pro and the 6.7 inch iphone  pro max which makes total sense and this  is actually based on ross young's  excellent excellent display leaks  because ross young has a 100 percent  accuracy rating with displays so he's  very very good now check out this chart  ross young believes that there's going  to be four different iphone models next  year there's going to be the regular 6.1  inch iphone 14 but then there's going to  be an iphone 14 max so it's going to get  the larger display but it's not going to  get all of the extra features and then  of course you got the iphone 14 pro and  the 14 pro max with no mini size at all  but if we take a closer look at this  chart we can see some very interesting  details what ross is basically  confirming is that both the regular  iphone 14 and 14 max models will still  get the regular face id with the current  iphone 13 notch however both of the pro  models the pro and the pro max are going  to be getting the new under display face  id system with the cutout and if we go  back to dylan dkt's tweet just a couple  of days ago he said that the face id  hardware will be placed underneath the  display basically exactly what ross  young said so if we go to shrimp apple  pro's leak it looks like this extra  cutout on the side is actually going to  be unnecessary so that leaves us with a  perfectly centered pill shaped cutout  and with that said the big question we  have to answer is how exactly is apple  gonna put the face id hardware under the  display so let's go ahead and explain  how that is going to work by looking at  the original iphone 10s face id system  as you can see in this image of the  entire truedepth sensor array for face  id we of course have the infrared camera  then the proximity sensor the flood  illuminator the ambient light sensor the  speaker the microphone the camera and  the dot projector so first of all we  know that the speaker and microphone are  already out of the notch they're all the  way up to the top of the display on the  iphone 13 but we still have those other  facility sensors that we have to put  underneath the display and before we get  into it the most important thing to  understand about face id is that it  works using an infrared camera system so  for example  both the flood illuminator and the dot  projector  shine infrared light onto your face as  you can see in this video example and  that detail is extremely important for  enabling apple to put it underneath the  display so for example we see the  original face id sensor right here the  dot projector the flood illuminator and  everything else however apple made some  major changes to the design of the  iphone 13's notch as you can see right  here in ifixit's tear down one thing  they mentioned is that the notch is now  20 percent narrower on the 13 pro  compared to the 12 pro which you can see  basically right here look how much  narrow it is boom 13 right there and  that's the 12 much longer and the reason  they're able to do that is because apple  was able to merge the flood illuminator  and the dot projector into a single  module as you can see right here with  the new iphone 13 and that's the old  iphone 12 design so here's what i  believe apple is gonna do with the new  iphone 14 pro design they're going to  take that new dot projector and flood  illuminator single module and then  they're going to stick it under the  display right there because it works  using infrared light so behind the  display it's still going to be able to  shine those dots and the light onto your  face and make face id work which is very  very important so now if we go back to  the original face id system both the dot  projector and flood illuminator are now  going to be under the display on top of  that the speaker and microphone are gone  leaving just the camera the infrared  camera and the ambient light in  proximity sensors and that brings us to  the next very important detail if you  look at this image of the iphone 13  display panel you'll see some light  leaking behind this little area on the  display and guess what with the iphone  13 apple was able to put the ambient  light sensor completely underneath the  display so if you look at that the only  things remaining are the camera the  infrared camera and the proximity sensor  so with all that said i found this  little image on twitter showing the new  pill-shaped cutout with all the  components within it and some of them  are actually wrong because the ambient  light sensor is not within the whole  punch it's actually underneath the  display and i believe that the dot  projector is also going to be underneath  the display alongside with the flood  illuminator leaving only the front  camera the infrared camera because it's  gonna have a hard time reading it and  potentially the proximity sensor so yeah  that's how i think apple is going to  pull this off with this pill-shaped  cutout which i think makes a lot of  sense because no other android phone had  a pill shaped cutout centered like this  and i think this design looks really  good and i think this is going to be a  really good choice for apple to do and i  personally believe that apple is going  to stick to this design for the next  couple of years until they can finally  put all of it under the display which is  going to be very difficult especially  the selfie camera but we might see it in  a couple of years and of course the  regular iphone 14 models are gonna have  the same old notch from the iphone 13.  and finally to finish off this video  let's get into my predictions for the  design of the iphone 14 pro and renders  by shailesh helped me out with some  custom renders that are based on of  course the designs from john prosser and  ian's elbow with this awesome looking  iphone 4s style design with the circular  buttons and of course the cover glass  extending both ways and along with that  i also took some rumors from dylan dkt  who believes that apple is going to  remove the physical sim card with the  iphone 14 pro models at least and here  we go here is the reveal of the renders  and bam that's the iphone 14 pro or at  least what i believe is gonna look like  there's no sim card tray you have the  glass extending out the front and the  back except i personally believe that  the camera bump is still going to stick  out a little bit further than the glass  compared to having it flush like john  prosser believes and of course we have  the new pill shaped cutout with the  camera on the left side so that is my  design for the iphone 14 pro and if you  guys completely disagree with me go  ahead and comment down below but i think  this looks absolutely beautiful and i  would pay more than a thousand dollars  for this design if they upped the price  which i think they're gonna do so  hopefully you guys enjoy this and if you  did go ahead and click the circle above  to subscribe for more videos like this  one check out one of those two right  over there thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video  [Music]
 

